      "content": "For structural integrity, ensure that environmental conditions such as moisture and temperature are controlled, as wood can warp or degrade over time. When spacing your joists, follow the manufacturer's recommendations and adhere to local building code requirements, which typically provide minimum spacing and bearing lengths to ensure load distribution. Regularly inspect your deck for signs of wear, such as loose fasteners or planed-through ends, and be cautious not to remove more material than allowed by the capacity of the joists. Consider adding joist hangers or brackets to increase the support at key points. Where possible, perform structural inspections with a qualified inspector to ensure everything is in order. Adopting engineered wood products like laminated veneer lumber (LVL) or glulam may enhance durability and strength compared to solid timber.",
